ger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">&lt;=
span&gt;</code>, React destroys the old tree and builds new one</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Stable tree structure</=
strong> - UI structure rarely changes drastically between renders</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Keys provide identity h=
ints</strong> - Developers can hint at element identity across renders</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Developer implications:<=
/strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Positive impacts:</stron=
g></p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Predictable performance=
</strong>: O(n) means linear scaling with tree size</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Real-time rendering</st=
rong>: Enables 60fps updates even with large component trees</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Simple mental model</st=
rong>: Developers can reason about performance linearly</li>
</ul>
