<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Real-world performance i=
mplications:</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">In the trading platform I built,=
 we had components rendering thousands of financial instruments. The O(n) g=
uarantee meant we could confidently update the entire list 60 times per sec=
ond without performance degradation, as long as we maintained stable keys a=
nd component structure.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Pe=
rfect! That shows deep understanding of the algorithmic trade-offs. Now, le=
t's talk about React 18's Concurrent Features. How does the new automatic b=
atching and time slicing change the update mechanism we just discussed?</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: Reac=
t 18's Concurrent Features represent a <strong>paradigm shift</strong> from=
 synchronous to <strong>interruptible, prioritized rendering</strong>. This=
 fundamentally changes how updates flow through the system.</p>
